READ-ONLY research spike. No package change, no version bump, no PR.
Five generating scripts + five NDJSON artifacts under `docs/srmech/notes/`
so no number below dangles (`[[feedback_computational_provenance_discipline]]`).
All measurements run on 0.9.0rc424 under WSL2 with numpy ABSENT.

MEASURED, not asserted:

* P1 — **0 of 29 carriers and 0 of 612 ops name a notation object.** The
  notation layer is EMPTY. rc424's music lane is RELATIONS (6 ops), one rung
  below. Of its 6 relational ops, 3 are frame-parametric / frame-free and 3
  hard-wire ℤ/12 — and they reach it through PRIVATE HELPERS, so a
  non-transitive audit under-reports it (the first version of this script did
  exactly that and the correction is left visible in the source).

* P2 — the GIS axioms EXECUTED. ℤ/n is a torsor at every n in
  {5,7,12,17,19,22,24,31,53} — **12 is not special.** The 24 consonant triads
  under T/I (NON-abelian, 360/576 non-commuting pairs) are a torsor
  13824/13824 + 576/576. Reversing the composition order breaks axiom A
  (5184/13824) while simple transitivity survives BOTH ways: **"is it a
  torsor" and "does axiom A hold" separate once IVLS is non-abelian**, and
  every abelian row is structurally blind to that. 4 negative controls, 0
  wrongly blessed.

* P3 — `octonion_frame_read` satisfies the CLEF SHAPE on all 28 frames:
  something moves (11 of 12 fields), something survives (`norm_sq`, 1/28), and
  NO frame-free quantity singles out the default frame. But the frame set is
  **not one torsor**: within a line the 8 signed base units act transitively
  with multiplicity 2 (stabiliser {±1}), so it is a torsor for the order-4
  QUOTIENT; across lines nothing shipped certifies one.
  `oct_torsor_*`'s group is measured to be **Q8** — order 8, non-abelian, one
  involution — and **0 of 7 candidate pitch-interval groups can be hosted**.

* P4 — octave equivalence IS the shipped central extension. `center_lift`'s
  shadow is bit-identical to the `cyclic_mod_add` chain at 10/10 moduli, and
  `lift_fibre` ENUMERATES the register coset. The origin torsor's group is
  ℤ, not ℤ/n (0/25 vs 25/25). Plus an executable three-bucket LEAK TEST that
  catches the three shipped ℤ/12 ops — so it can return otherwise.

* P5 — the carrier+chart prototype, and it **falsified its own first atlas
  test**: checking chart compatibility THROUGH the carrier blessed a
  deliberately corrupted chart 1225/1225. Retained rather than deleted,
  because the lesson is the deliverable — an atlas's content lives entirely
  in TRANSITION MAPS, which must be supplied and checked, never inferred.
  Under the corrected condition the corrupted chart fails (30/35), and the
  derived transition for an origin shift produced the KEY-SIGNATURE shape
  unprompted: rotate the alphabet by 3, one degree of seven needs a flat.

